From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhugengyu <zhugengyu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] sdio: (recv) Drop the frame when the RX copy allocation
 fails

When the per-frame copy cannot be allocated, the SDIO receive path falls
back to cloning the receive buffer's skb.  Under CONFIG_SDIO_RX_COPY that
clone cannot represent the frame: its data pointer addresses the start of
the whole read buffer rather than this frame's pdata, and its length is the
whole read.  The indication path then hands the read buffer to the stack as
one oversized ethernet frame instead of the frame that arrived.

There is nothing to deliver when the copy fails.  Drop the frame and let
the transport retransmit it.

Signed-off-by: zhugengyu <zhugengyu@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 os_dep/linux/recv_linux.c | 29 ++++++++++++-----------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

--- a/os_dep/linux/recv_linux.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/recv_linux.c
@@ -125,29 +125,18 @@
 
 		res = _FAIL;
 #else
-		if ((pattrib->mfrag == 1) && (pattrib->frag_num == 0)) {
-			RTW_INFO("%s: alloc_skb fail , drop frag frame\n", __FUNCTION__);
-			/* rtw_free_recvframe(precvframe, pfree_recv_queue); */
-			res = _FAIL;
-			goto exit_rtw_os_recv_resource_alloc;
-		}
-
-		if (pskb == NULL) {
-			res = _FAIL;
-			goto exit_rtw_os_recv_resource_alloc;
-		}
-
-		precvframe->u.hdr.pkt = rtw_skb_clone(pskb);
-		if (precvframe->u.hdr.pkt) {
-			precvframe->u.hdr.pkt->dev = padapter->pnetdev;
-			precvframe->u.hdr.rx_head = precvframe->u.hdr.rx_data = precvframe->u.hdr.rx_tail = pdata;
-			precvframe->u.hdr.rx_end =  pdata + alloc_sz;
-		} else {
-			RTW_INFO("%s: rtw_skb_clone fail\n", __FUNCTION__);
-			/* rtw_free_recvframe(precvframe, pfree_recv_queue); */
-			/*exit_rtw_os_recv_resource_alloc;*/
-			res = _FAIL;
-		}
+		/*
+		 * The copy failed, so there is no frame to hand upward.  Do not
+		 * fall back to cloning the receive buffer: a clone's data pointer
+		 * addresses the start of the whole read buffer rather than this
+		 * frame's pdata, and its length is the whole read, so the stack
+		 * would receive the read buffer as one oversized ethernet frame.
+		 * Dropping the frame costs a retransmission; the clone delivers a
+		 * frame that was never received.
+		 */
+		RTW_INFO("%s: alloc_skb fail, drop frame\n", __FUNCTION__);
+		precvframe->u.hdr.pkt = NULL;
+		res = _FAIL;
 #endif
 	}
 
